# eSim Tool Manager (`etm`)

A Linux-first CLI tool for managing Electronic Design Automation (EDA) dependencies for eSim.

[![Python 3.11+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.11+-3776AB.svg?style=flat-square&logo=python&logoColor=white)](https://www.python.org/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg?style=flat-square)](LICENSE)
[![CI Pipeline](https://img.shields.io/github/actions/workflow/status/csyuvraj/esim-tool-manager/ci.yml?branch=main&label=CI&style=flat-square&logo=github)](https://github.com/csyuvraj/esim-tool-manager/actions)

---

## Why this project?

Setting up eSim dependencies manually gets repetitive fast. Remembering exact APT package names for tools like Ngspice or KiCad, checking if binaries are already installed, and reading install logs shouldn't require custom shell scripts.

`etm` wraps those setup and diagnostic tasks into a single CLI tool. It gives you a clean view of your installed EDA tools, runs health checks on your environment, and manages installs safely through an OS-aware package manager interface.

---

## Features

* **Tool Registry:** Reads tool metadata and binary names directly from `tool_manager/data/tools.yaml`.
* **OS-Aware Package Dispatch:** Uses `AptManager` on Linux and safely falls back to `DummyPackageManager` on unsupported systems.
* **System Diagnostics:** Runs environment and package manager checks with `etm doctor`.
* **Terminal UI:** Displays status tables, logs, and command outputs using Typer and Rich.
* **Execution Logging:** Records command activity using Python's standard `logging` library.

---

## Installation

Clone the repository and install it in editable mode:

```bash
git clone [https://github.com/csyuvraj/esim-tool-manager.git](https://github.com/csyuvraj/esim-tool-manager.git)
cd esim-tool-manager

python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate

pip install -e .
